<title>USA: Motorola gets $54 million India contract.</title>
<headline>Motorola gets $54 million India contract.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc's International Cellular Infrastructure Group said Monday it signed a nearly $54 million contract to deploy digital cellular telephone networks in India.</p>
<p>Motorola's global system for mobile communications (GSM) service is expected to be available for subscribers in Karnataka and Punjab by the end of 1996.</p>
<p>The contract is with Modicom Network Private Limited.  Under the agreement, Motorola will install its InCell GSM base and provide technical support.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
